local _, ns = ...

ns.WhatsNew = {
    { version = "7.0.6", text = "More control over fading, a stack of nameplate options you asked for, and Korean and German translations by a player.\n\n|cffffd100Heads up|r\nSome things look or work differently even if you change nothing:\n• |cffffffffNameplates:|r the cast bar has its own |cffffffffBar Texture|r and |cffffffffBorder|r now, FlareUI Dark and FlareUI Thin to start. It no longer copies the plate's texture and border, so set them again on the Cast Bar tab if you changed the plate's.\n• |cffffffffNameplates:|r the plate under your mouse gets a lighter border and bar. Pick what lights up, or turn it off, with |cffffffffMouseover Highlight|r on the Targeting tab.\n• |cffffffffLoot Window:|r with auto loot on, FlareUI's loot window opens for a moment like Blizzard's, and the items leave it as you pick them up.\n\n|cffffd100Highlights|r\n• |cffffffffFade Delay|r on every frame that fades by your choice.\n• |cffffffffNameplates:|r class-coloured names, guild colours, titles and a separate cast bar look.\n• |cffffffffKorean|r and |cffffffffGerman|r translations by ithiel.\n\n|cffffd100New|r\n\n|cffe6cc99Fading|r\n• |cffffffffFade Delay|r (0 seconds) in the Fading section of Edit Mode: how long a frame stays after its last reason to show, before it fades.\n      - On the action bars (1–8, pet, stance, Totem Bar), the gryphons, the bags bar, the micro menu, the player and pet frames, the Resource Bars' Health, Power, Mana and Combo Points, the XP bar, the minimap, Buffs, Debuffs, the Quest Tracker and the Cooldown Manager.\n      - In a fade group the whole group shares one delay.\n      - Frames the game shows and hides by itself (target, focus, the cast bar and similar) don't have it.\n• |cffffffffSlower|r Hide Speed: fades to about half over 2 seconds, waits 2 seconds, then fades out. By themese.\n\n|cffe6cc99Chat|r\n• |cffffffffKeep Messages Shown|r (off) in the chat's Edit Mode Fading section, after Fade Old Lines: the window, tabs and buttons fade as set, but the messages stay readable.\n\n|cffe6cc99Nameplates|r\n• |cffffffffColour Names by Class|r (off) on the Plate tab: players' names on full plates in their class colour.\n• |cffffffffColour Guild Members|r (off, Friendly Player): your guild's names in Blizzard's guild green on Name Only plates.\n• |cffffffffShow Titles|r: players' titles and NPC roles under the name. On for NPCs, off for players and Minor.\n• |cffffffffBar Texture|r and |cffffffffBorder|r for the cast bar, on the Cast Bar tab above Cast Bar Height.\n• |cffffffffMouseover Highlight|r on the Targeting tab, under Target Highlight: tick |cffffffffBorder|r, |cffffffffBar|r and |cffffffffOuter Glow|r (Border and Bar to start).\n\n|cffe6cc99Radial Menu|r\n• |cffffffffTanning|r and |cffffffffBait and Tackle|r in the Professions list.\n\n|cffe6cc99Translations|r\n• |cffffffffKorean|r and |cffffffffGerman|r, by ithiel.\n\n|cffffd100Changed|r\n• |cffffffffNameplates:|r\n      - |cffffffffHeight|r goes down to 5.\n      - The tab row is split into two labelled groups: |cffffffffThis Unit Type|r and |cffffffffAll Nameplates|r.\n      - The mouseover highlight also lightens the target and threat border colours.\n      - |cffffffffShow Full Name|r is hidden for NPC types, where it did nothing.\n      - Plates update more cheaply in big pulls. By parchinskiy.\n• |cffffffffParty Frames:|r in the Gamepad UI, the target highlight is twice as bright, to spot the member picked with the D-pad.\n• |cffffffffMeters:|r the Cyrillic font is used only for names with Russian letters.\n• |cffffffffFrench:|r the 7.0.4 and 7.0.5 text translated. By Brainc3ll.\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n• |cffffffffGamepad UI:|r party targeting with LB and the D-pad didn't work if the Gamepad UI was switched on after login. |cffffffffController players, please tell us if it works for you now.|r\n• |cffffffffUnit Frames:|r |cffffffffValues on Mouseover|r with a druid's |cffffffffMana on Shapeshift|r hid all the numbers in caster form.\n• |cffffffffBuff Reminders:|r the food reminder remembered a drink as your food. By GregDuhamel.\n• |cffffffffLoot Window:|r the gap above the first row now matches the sides." },
    { version = "7.0.5", text = "Two new windows from the community: a FlareUI loot window and a searchable flight list. Pet threat on nameplates, the same Health Text picker on raid frames, and a stack of fixes.\n\n|cffffffffRestart the game fully after updating|r (not just /reload): this version adds new files.\n\n|cffffd100Heads up|r\nSome things look or work differently even if you change nothing:\n• |cffffffffLoot Roll Window:|r |cffffffffBackground Opacity|r is gone. The window always shows at full strength, since it was hard to read see-through.\n• |cffffffffQuality of Life:|r |cffffffffCoordinates on the World Map|r is gone from Map & Mail. It only switched Blizzard's own map coordinates, which are still in Blizzard's options (Interface).\n• |cffffffffNameplates:|r |cffffffffThreat Percentage|r no longer takes the level's place. It has its own small box beside the plate.\n\n|cffffd100Highlights|r\n• |cffffffffLoot Window:|r FlareUI's own window for corpses and chests.\n• |cffffffffFlight Destination List:|r search the flight map by stop or zone.\n• |cffffffffNameplates:|r your pet's threat counts.\n\n|cffffd100New|r\n\n|cffe6cc99Bags & Looting|r\n• |cffffffffLoot Window|r (off) on the Looting tab: FlareUI's loot window replaces Blizzard's for corpses and chests. By Xentinus.\n      - Shows how many of each item you already carry.\n      - Item marks follow your Bags options: item level, junk coin, BoE, uncollected appearances, thin or thick borders and rarity colours.\n      - A looted item leaves a gap, so nothing moves under your mouse.\n      - Placed and scaled in Edit Mode as \"FlareUI Loot Window\".\n• |cffffffffShow Free Bag Slots|r (off): your free bag slots at the bottom of the loot window, red when the bags are full.\n\n|cffe6cc99Quality of Life|r\n• |cffffffffFlight Destination List|r (off) in Map & Mail: a list beside the flight map. By parchinskiy.\n      - Search for a stop by name or zone.\n      - See each fare.\n      - Star the stops you use most to keep them at the top, for each character.\n\n|cffe6cc99Nameplates|r\n• |cffffffffPet threat:|r a mob your pet holds takes the |cffffffffAnother Tank Has It|r colour, for tanks and damage dealers alike.\n• |cffffffffDoesItDie|r and |cffffffffDoesItDiePlus|r show their marker on FlareUI's nameplates. DoesItDiePlus works on the target and focus frames too (by BillChirico).\n\n|cffffd100Changed|r\n• |cffffffffNameplates:|r |cffffffffThreat Percentage|r sits in its own small box, on the side away from the level, or on the right with no level.\n• |cffffffffParty Frames:|r in Raid Style, |cffffffffHealth Text|r and |cffffffffPower Text|r use the same picker as the other frames, with the Centre slot only. Your old choice carries over.\n• |cffffffffRaid Frames:|r |cffffffffHealth Text|r and |cffffffffPower Text|r use the same Centre-only picker. Your old choice carries over.\n• |cffffffffQuest Tracker:|r the header buttons are bronze icons instead of boxes, by GregDuhamel. They follow your |cffffffffColour Scheme|r: bronze with FlareUI's, gold with Blizzard's.\n• |cffffffffMeters:|r if Blizzard's own meter Visibility is set to In a Group or Hidden, a window at login explains why the meter hides in a fight and opens Edit Mode to fix it. Blizzard's Visibility row now stays in the meter's Edit Mode dialog while it is wrong.\n• |cffffffffSettings:|r new previews in the info panel:\n      - the loot window\n      - the Quest Tracker's Colour Scheme, header buttons, complete tag and scroll bar\n      - the chat's Frame Style, edit box, icons, header buttons and tab glow\n      - the bags' item level, BoE, uncollected and empty slots\n      - the minimap's Info Bar\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n• |cffffffffChat:|r chat tabs couldn't be switched during a fight.\n• |cffffffffParty Frames:|r after switching from Classic to Raid Style, the old health text showed beside the new one.\n• |cffffffffBags:|r using a reagent from the crafting bag in the backpack (an armor kit, filling a crate) could be blocked. By parchinskiy.\n• |cffffffffResource Bars:|r a /reload during a flight broke the Resource Bars until the next reload. By GregDuhamel.\n• |cffffffffSettings:|r a section's Reset skipped six options: Button Scale, XP Bubbles, Gryphons, Food and Flask, Hide for My Role and Auto Minimize. By GregDuhamel.\n• |cffffffffSettings:|r Buff Reminders showed no previews.\n• |cffffffffProfiles:|r importing a profile now checks every option's value type. By GregDuhamel." },
    { version = "7.0.4", text = "A big batch from your ideas: names above the nameplates, Blizzard's cast bar glow, stacked buffs and debuffs, and item levels in the inspect window. It also brings smoother nameplates in big pulls and the normal game font back.\n\n|cffffd100Heads up|r\nSome things look or work differently even if you change nothing:\n• |cffffffffFonts:|r the game font is back to normal. 7.0.3 swapped it for Blizzard's Russian copy by accident, which looked sharper and drew some symbols as boxes. Liked the sharper look? Pick |cffffffffFriz Quadrata TT (Crisp)|r in any font list.\n• |cffffffffNameplates:|r Name Only plates show players' full names. Switch |cffffffffShow Full Name|r off for first names only.\n• |cffffffffUnit Frames:|r |cffffffffName Above Plates|r is now called |cffffffffName Above Frames|r.\n\n|cffffd100Highlights|r\n• |cffffffffNameplates:|r names above the plate, and smoother plates in big pulls.\n• |cffffffffCast bars:|r Blizzard's bright edge at the front of the cast.\n• |cffffffffBuffs and Debuffs|r can share a place on the unit, party and boss frames.\n\n|cffffd100New|r\n\n|cffe6cc99Nameplates|r\n• |cffffffffNames Above Plate|r (Off) on the Style tab: the name above the plate, left, centre or right, first or full name. Buffs and debuffs move up to make room.\n• |cffffffffShow Full Name|r (on) in the Name Only Mode section.\n• |cffffffffEdge Glow|r on the Cast Bar tab.\n\n|cffe6cc99Cast Bars|r\n• |cffffffffEdge Glow|r: a bright edge at the front of the cast, as on Blizzard's cast bars.\n      - In each frame's Cast Bar section in Edit Mode, and under Look on the Player Cast Bar.\n      - On for new players. Already using FlareUI? Switch it on there.\n\n|cffe6cc99Unit Frames|r\n• |cffffffffBuffs|r and |cffffffffDebuffs|r can pick the same place, or the same edge: they stack. The one placed first stays next to the frame, the other goes one row further out. Party and boss frames too.\n• |cffffffffRange Check|r (off) on Target of Target and Target of Focus.\n\n|cffe6cc99Resource Bars|r\n• |cffffffffShow in Caster Form|r (off) on the Druid Mana bar: it stays up in caster form too.\n\n|cffe6cc99Bags|r\n• |cffffffffReverse Bag Fill|r (off): the backpack starts at the top left and fills left to right, downwards.\n• |cffffffffItem Level|r also shows on the inspect window's slots, with the player's average item level under their name.\n\n|cffe6cc99Minimap|r\n• |cffffffffBelow the Map|r (off) in the Info Bar section: the bar sits under the minimap, clear of the quest arrow.\n\n|cffe6cc99Meters|r\n• |cffffffffHide Until Next Group|r in the meter's gear menu: the meter goes away until you join another group, or reload.\n\n|cffe6cc99Fonts|r\n• |cffffffffFriz Quadrata TT (Crisp)|r: Blizzard's sharper copy of the game font. It lacks a few symbols.\n\n|cffffd100Changed|r\n• |cffffffffNameplates:|r the Visibility tab works with the Nameplates module off. Those are Blizzard's own nameplate settings, so you can switch In Combat back off.\n• |cffffffffNameplates:|r the settings preview shows aura timers and swipes.\n• |cffffffffAction Bars:|r |cffffffffUpdate Spell Ranks|r moves your pet's spells up too (a warlock's Torment after the grimoire).\n• |cffffffffBuffs & Debuffs:|r |cffffffffFiltered Auras|r marks debuffs the game won't let addons hide on you as |cffffffffNot on You|r.\n• |cffffffffRadial Menu:|r a |cffffd100/click FUIRadial|r macro opens the radial for the controller while the Gamepad UI is on.\n• |cffffffffAbout:|r Kabaday is credited for the loot roll window and the Cooldown Manager.\n• |cffffffffFrench:|r the 7.0.2 and 7.0.3 text is translated. By Brainc3ll.\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n• |cffffffffQuest Tracker:|r with Blizzard's Gamepad UI on, a mouse click on a quest showed \"Open your quest log\" instead of opening it.\n• |cffffffffQuest Tracker:|r quests that Blizzard's own tracker doesn't list open on a click too.\n• |cffffffffNameplates:|r less stutter in big pulls. Out of Range Opacity, threat colours and glows do far less work per mob.\n• |cffffffffFonts:|r tooltips showed boxes instead of the \"·\" dot." },
    { version = "7.0.3", text = "More nameplate polish, plus fixes for the bugs you sent in after 7.0.2. Nameplate auras get their own look options and can stack in two lines.\n\n|cffffd100Heads up|r\nSome things look or work differently even if you change nothing:\n• |cffffffffNameplates:|r player names on full plates are white. Class colour stays on Name Only plates, where it is easy to read.\n• |cffffffffNameplates:|r |cffffffffThreat Percentage|r no longer sits over the name. It shows in the level box instead of the level while you have threat. With |cffffffffLevel|r off, it gets its own small box right of the plate, shown only in a fight.\n• |cffffffffNameplates:|r the raid marker sits on the side opposite the quest icon. |cffffffffDefensives|r and |cffffffffCrowd Control|r go past it on its side.\n\n|cffffd100New|r\n\n|cffe6cc99Nameplates|r\n• |cffffffffAuras|r section at the top of the Auras tab, for each plate type:\n      - |cffffffffAura Icon Shape|r (Square)\n      - |cffffffffAura Swipe|r, |cffffffffAura Timer|r and |cffffffffTimer Colour|r: start with your Unit Frames values, so nothing changes.\n• |cffffffffAura Positions|r section below Debuffs, shown when both Buffs and Debuffs are on:\n      - |cffffffffPosition|r (One Line): |cffffffffOne Line|r keeps them side by side, as before.\n      - |cffffffffBuffs on Top|r or |cffffffffDebuffs on Top|r: each gets its own line across the whole plate, one line at most.\n\n|cffffd100Changed|r\n• |cffffffffNameplates:|r |cffffffffQuest Objective|r and |cffffffffQuest Progress|r no longer show for the two player plate types.\n• |cffffffffFrench:|r the 7.0.1 text is translated. By Brainc3ll.\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n• |cffffffffChat:|r with |cffffffffFade Old Lines|r on, names are clickable again and link tooltips no longer flicker.\n• |cffffffffUnit Frames:|r |cffffffffValues on Mouseover|r works on the player frame again. Other frames no longer need one hover after Edit Mode.\n• |cffffffffBags & Looting:|r a switched-off module stays off after a reload.\n• |cffffffffFonts:|r Russian names show in the meter on English clients. FlareUI uses Blizzard's Cyrillic fonts where the game has them. Fix from Aleksandr Vasinskyi.\n• |cffffffffBuffs & Debuffs:|r the |cffffffffPick One of Yours|r list no longer errors in a fight." },
    { version = "7.0.2", text = "A quick hotfix for four things 7.0.1 broke or missed. Thanks for reporting them so fast.\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n• |cffffffffQuest Tracker:|r a left click on a quest opens it again. 7.0.1 only showed \"Open your quest log to read this quest\" for most quests.\n• |cffffffffBags:|r the crafting bag shows its items in the combined backpack again (|cffffffffCrafting Bag in Backpack|r). 7.0.1 left the section empty when you opened only the backpack.\n• |cffffffffNameplates:|r |cffffffffFull Name|r is a choice in the plate's |cffffffffHealth Text|r, so friendly players can show their surname. 7.0.1 drew it but left it out of the list.\n• |cffffffffNameplates:|r the raid marker sits right beside full plates. The |cffffffffDefensives|r icons now go past it instead of pushing it far to the left." },
}
